Z||000005||DR650SE||11-27-2001||11:38 AM||||Friend=7<BR>Roger Do you have the hooters address?  I need it for a guy from the fiero mailing list.  He doesnt want to sit around in town and get stuck cuz his turbo will get hot.  If he can come that will make seven.  I want to try and get him the directions asap.  All I neewd is the address.  Or if you can help, here is the letter he sent me.  Im not too familiar with the area.<BR>---------------------------------------------<BR>I dont want to get lost in Columbus,my turbo gets hot in traffic.So i need some step by step directions here.<BR>I will be coming 77 south to 70 west where am i going after that?  <BR>E-mail:  et1320n12@lycos.com<P>****BRING CAMERA"S SO WE CAN POST PICS!!****<p>[This message has been edited by DR650SE (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||11-27-2001||10:28 PM||||very ez, not 1 stop lite at all. when he gets to 70 west, its about an hour & 15 mins till he gets to the east side of Columbus. after he passes Brice Rd exit, I-270 north is next exit to the right. the first exit on 270 north is Main St east to the right. as you come off the exit Hooters is rite beside you on the right. after you stop at the exit turn right into the right lane and then another right at first road, then immediately turn right into the driveway. I think the address is 6000 E main st. phone is (614) 755-9464.||||reg||1
